    "durationMs": 174384,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what was built:\n\n**Implementation** (Laravel 11, PHP 8.3, in `/workspace`):\n- `POST /links` — validates `url` (absolute http/https with host via `parse_url`) and optional `code` (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`); auto-generates a unique 8-char code when omitted; returns `201 {\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the submitted URL unchanged; `409 {\"error\":...}` for duplicate codes (pre-check plus a unique-index race guard), `422 {\"error\":...}` for bad input\n- `GET /links/{code}` — `200` with the link or `404 {\"error\":...}`\n- `GET /r/{code}` — `302` with `Location` set to the stored URL, atomic `increment('clicks')` so each request counts exactly once; `404` for unknown codes\n- `GET /links` — `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}` in ascending creation order\n- Malformed JSON and all validation failures return `422` JSON with an `error` field (custom `ValidationException` renderer in `bootstrap/app.php`)\n- `routes/api.php` registered with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}`, not `/api/*`\n- Eloquent `Link` model + MySQL migration (`code` unique with `utf8mb4_bin` for exact-match semantics, `clicks` default 0); DB settings come solely from `DB_*` env vars — `.env` contains no credentials\n- `start.sh` runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload`; README explains startup\n\n**Verified by live HTTP tests**: all endpoint responses and status codes, duplicate 409, every 422 case (missing/invalid url, short/long/invalid-char code, malformed JSON), unknown-code 404s, and a full server restart showing links and click counts persist in MySQL. Test data was truncated and the server stopped so the automated suite starts clean on port 8000."
